{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-species-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.74, step 7f. `scale-county-timeagg-year-minor-species`: `scale-county-timeagg-year`'s Year collapse (January, April, July and October 2020, both day types, all 24 hours, road types 1 and 4 -- MOVES adds 2, 3 and 5 for running exhaust's off-network idle -- source types 21 and 62, `inputs/washtenaw-county-timeagg.esm`, VMT output on) selecting `scale-county-minor-species`'s species unchanged: the PM species (100, 110, 111, 112, 115, 118, 119, 35, 36, 51-59, 121-124) and the PAH particles (23, 68-78, 81-84) at running, start, extended idle, APU and crankcase running, start and extended idle, and the metals and dioxins/furans at running exhaust. MOVESOutput is 75,582 rows, the Hour twin's key set: 38 pollutants at the seven processes, and no metal or dioxin row (no `sourceTypePolProcess` row, so no source-bin distribution and no distance-rate weighting).\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the Hour twin's arithmetic -- SulfatePMCalculator's pmSpeciation outputs, TOM and the residual, its crankcase split onto the crankcase processes, AirToxicsCalculator's PAH particles from organic carbon at the same process -- over PreAggYEAR.sql's month collapse, whose summed FuelSupply SulfatePMCalculator reads as a sum (F69).\n\n`n_aggregatesMonths` is 1; `db_aggregationmonth` and `db_rateday` are read from its XML by `tools/runspec-month-selection.py` and `tools/runspec-day-selection.py`. `n_outputRate` is bound to 75582; `n_physicsRow` 21, the two source types' physics rows.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "hotelling-adjustment",
      "crankcase",
      "pm-speciation",
      "air-toxics",
      "running-exhaust",
      "start-exhaust",
      "time-aggregation"
    ]
  },
